I deviate from “make the callout right from the trigger” for bulk inserts: a 200-account batch would require 200 HTTP callouts in the same DML transaction, which exceeds Salesforce per-transaction callout limits and makes account creation depend on ERP availability. I keep a direct callout for the single-account user flow, and for larger batches I enqueue queueable work in small chunks while still sending one HTTP request per account.

